{"kind":"report","text":"Planner decision for b32b2f16 (P1: the stricter version 2 reader against the published Grow demo packet 71e10ca9).\n\nContext: the hosted Grow room is being provisioned now, on its own Worker, from main 8aad37bb, with release 71e10ca9 installed. After that, a reader that cannot open the packet would break a live room on its next host deployment.\n\nAdopted: option A, with bounds. P1 lands with the stricter reader for everything new. dap pack and validatePackage enforce the seven composition members, and no new packet is produced in the earlier shape. Reading a packet that is already signed in the earlier version 2 shape stays possible through one explicit boundary, used only to verify, install, deliver screens and replay a published packet. It is strict for that shape: it is selected by a stated rule, not by lenient parsing, and it keeps every graph refusal. The tests read the actual committed bytes of the demo packet through that boundary, and show that a new packet without the composition members is refused by pack and validation. Document the boundary and the shape it reads in the package documentation, and say which later release retires it.\n\nThe boundary is retired by a later reviewed replacement release of the demo, with its own trust row and an upgrade of the installed room, filed when the planner asks for it. It is not part of P1. No signing with the existing publisher key, no change to demo bytes, and no deployment is granted here.","body":{"to":"builder"}}